cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hybrid Hidden Markov–Copula Precipitation Framework"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as follows."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Herrera-Marín
    given-names: Mauricio
repository-code: "https://github.com/mauricio-herrera/hybrid-nhmm-copula-precipitation-framework"
abstract: >
  Hierarchical framework integrating non-homogeneous Hidden Markov Models (nHMM),
  Dynamic Time Warping (DTW) clustering, and state-conditional Regular Vine (R-vine)
  copulas with Generalized Pareto (GPD) tails to characterize and simulate Chilean
  rainfall regimes (1980–2022). This repository includes compressed data, scripts,
  and reproducible diagnostics supporting the manuscript "Characterizing Climate-Driven
  Shifts in Chilean Rainfall Regimes with a Hybrid Hidden Markov–Copula Framework."
license: MIT
keywords:
  - nHMM
  - DTW
  - vine copulas
  - GPD
  - precipitation
  - Chile
  - rainfall regimes
  - hydroclimate
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-11-08"
